<title>GERMANY: Daimler says in talks on AEG Electrocom.</title>
<headline>Daimler says in talks on AEG Electrocom.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG is holding talks with several interested parties aimed at selling off at least part of its AEG Electrocom unit, Daimler spokesman Roland Klein said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Klein told Reuters a decision would be made by the end of the year but declined to name any of the interested parties.</p>
<p>He was reacting to an advance release from Monday's edition of the news magazine Der Spiegel which said the company wanted to sell AEG Electrocom, which makes mail sorting equipment.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, +49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
